      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would argue that migrate is the right word because the credentials are properly encrypted, they\u0027re just encrypted with an insecure known key.\n\nThis log is telling the operator to migrate *off* the insecure known key to a proper key repository via re-encryption. Migrations can be done whenever... they don\u0027t have to be done only once. I can migrate as much as my deployments security requirements mandate me to do so by doing: \n\n  1.) keystone-manage credential_rotate\n  2.) keystone-manage credential_migrate\n  3.) keystone-manage credential_rotate\n  4.) keystone-manage credential_migrate",
